[Unit]
Description=Quant heavy research organs -- one shared memory budget

# WHY A SLICE AND NOT MORE PER-UNIT CAPS (2026-09-01). Per-unit MemoryHigh fixed the units that
# were killing THEMSELVES: quant-queue-guard died 284x/day against a 200M cap it needed 271M for,
# and eleven units ran with MemoryMax=infinity on a swapless 3814MB box. Those are fixed.
#
# What per-unit caps CANNOT fix is the sum. Measured 2026-09-01 02:20: quant-external-panel was
# oom-killed at a 668M peak while its own ceiling was 800M -- it had not misbehaved at all. The
# BOX was at 138MB free / 397MB available, so the global OOM killer fired and chose the largest
# process it could see. Eighteen organs peak above 400M and several exceed 1G (manifest-dispatch
# 1536M, full-pipeline 1228M, cadence 1126M); nothing stops them coinciding, and when they do the
# victim is whoever happens to be biggest -- routinely a unit that fit perfectly well, and on this
# box sometimes the memecoin desk or a Claude session rather than a quant organ at all.
#
# A slice bounds the SUM. The organs inside it throttle each other under MemoryHigh -- reclaim
# first, slow down, still finish -- instead of the machine running out and the kernel picking a
# casualty from everything running on it. The budget is set with real headroom so nothing that
# fits today is newly constrained: this is a blast-radius bound, not a diet.
[Slice]
MemoryHigh=2400M
MemoryMax=2800M
MemorySwapMax=0
